Platformer Starter template — provenance and license
=====================================================

Content: engine-generated (original generated content of the Thirdlight
campaign). No downloaded asset, no third-party bytes; no license is
asserted over external material.

Derivation: this template is derived from the accepted Beacon Reach sample
recipe (samples/beacon-reach/recipe/commands.json — 26 commands, committed
with its generation tooling and asset provenance under samples/beacon-reach/).
The source assets below are byte-identical copies of the sample's
self-generated assets (samples/beacon-reach/assets/); their generation
scripts and provenance JSON are committed there. The recipe reuses the
sample's layout commands with the template's own game text (commands 1-26)
and adds (27-30) the courier modelAnimation binding, one decoration prefab
definition and two independent decoration prefab instances.

Digests: the descriptor's "blobs" inventory lists every source file with
its SHA-256 digest and byte length; the descriptor's recipeDigest/baseDigest/
contentDigest follow the accepted block-digest rule (SHA-256 of the canonical
2-space JSON + one trailing LF of the committed document; contentDigest over
the descriptor without its own contentDigest field).

Distribution: this directory is engine content (part of the engine
distribution; the packet-66 engine-kit layout owns its in-kit location).
Creating a project copies these bytes into the project's own content store
— the project never references this directory after creation.
